# graphify scope for the Inner Tepenia GDD knowledge graph.
#
# What the graph is for: the game's own content — lore, in-world history, the
# Tepenian universe, design and mechanics. Everything the project actually
# authored.
#
# What is deliberately out: source books, papers, treaties, and other
# real-world reference media. Those are reading material, not game content.
# What we need from them has already been extracted by hand into
# Reference/Real-World/ (and into the design files themselves), and that
# extracted material IS in scope. There is no value in graphing the PDFs and
# EPUBs themselves, and doing so would dominate extraction cost with noise.

# --- Real-world source media (44 GB of books, PDFs, and bundled sample code)
Reference/Materials/

# --- More real-world source media living outside Reference/ (95 PDFs, 19 EPUBs)
to-be-integrated/books/
to-be-integrated/treaties/

# --- graphify's own output
graphify-out/

# --- Explicitly kept in scope, for the record (no pattern needed, listed as
#     documentation of intent):
#       Worldspace/                 core lore, characters, factions, locations
#       Background-Lore/            per-city historical vignettes
#       Storyline/                  quests, endings, DLC
#       Neo-Races-and-Cultures/     culture catalogs
#       Game-Mechanics/             systems design
#       Reference/Real-World/       hand-extracted research (the useful residue
#                                   of the excluded source media)
#       Reference/Images/           maps and visual reference
#       Dev-Road-Map/, Code-Architecture/, Theoretical-Calculations/,
#       General-Overview-Notes/, to-be-integrated/ (minus books & treaties),
#       and the root logs (TODO.md, DONE.md, README.md)
